{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_delta","contentIndex":1,"delta":"{\"i\":\"Writing preflight report\",\"path\":\"in/db/preflight_report.md\",\"content\":\"# Preflight Report\\n\\n## Dirty email rows before migration\\n\\nSource data in `schema.sql` contains three email integrity violations in `users`:\\n\\n- Duplicate email: `u4` repeats `ada@example.com`, which is already used by `u1`.\\n- Null email: `u5` has `email = NULL`.\\n- Blank email: `u6` has `email = ''`.\\n\\nThese rows cannot satisfy a future `NOT NULL` plus unique email constraint without cleanup.\\n\\n## Required deterministic cleanup\\n\\nThe migration must preserve the rows and rewrite only the invalid email values to these deterministic values:\\n\\n- `u4` -> `ada+u4@example.com`\\n- `u5` -> `missing+u5@example.invalid`\\n- `u6` -> `missing+u6@example.invalid`\\n\\n`u1` keeps `ada@example.com` unchanged as the first valid holder of that address.\\n\\n## Dependent orders that must remain attached\\n\\nDirty users have dependent orders that must keep the same `user_id` values after migration:\\n\\n- `u4` -> order `o2`\\n- `u5` -> order `o3`\\n- `u6` -> order `o4`\\n\\nThe migration therefore must preserve user ids and rebuild `users` without deleting or rekeying those rows.\\n\"}"}}
{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":1,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_4Rhpgrdm79GnNglmvqBUD0gF|fc_05c07d1a95d865f8016a959fcd926887d29f3817d49a6e5c3f","name":"write","arguments":{"i":"Writing preflight report","path":"in/db/preflight_report.md","content":"# Preflight Report\n\n## Dirty email rows before migration\n\nSource data in `schema.sql` contains three email integrity violations in `users`:\n\n- Duplicate email: `u4` repeats `ada@example.com`, which is already used by `u1`.\n- Null email: `u5` has `email = NULL`.\n- Blank email: `u6` has `email = ''`.\n\nThese rows cannot satisfy a future `NOT NULL` plus unique email constraint without cleanup.\n\n## Required deterministic cleanup\n\nThe migration must preserve the rows and rewrite only the invalid email values to these deterministic values:\n\n- `u4` -> `ada+u4@example.com`\n- `u5` -> `missing+u5@example.invalid`\n- `u6` -> `missing+u6@example.invalid`\n\n`u1` keeps `ada@example.com` unchanged as the first valid holder of that address.\n\n## Dependent orders that must remain attached\n\nDirty users have dependent orders that must keep the same `user_id` values after migration:\n\n- `u4` -> order `o2`\n- `u5` -> order `o3`\n- `u6` -> order `o4`\n\nThe migration therefore must preserve user ids and rebuild `users` without deleting or rekeying those rows.\n"}}}}
