{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"Done.\n\nChanged:\n- `in/db/migration.sql`\n- `in/db/preflight_report.md`\n- `in/db/rollback.sql`\n- `in/db/postcheck.sql`\n- `in/db/migration_report.md`\n\nKey fixes:\n- Replaced the destructive `DROP TABLE users` draft with an explicit transactioned rebuild: `BEGIN IMMEDIATE ... COMMIT`.\n- Preserved all six users and all four orders.\n- Preserved `orders.user_id` values by rebuilding `users` with the same primary keys.\n- Preserved historical `created_at`.\n- Added `status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active'`.\n- Enforced future email integrity with `email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE` plus `idx_users_email`.\n- Applied the required deterministic cleanup:\n  - `u4 -> ada+u4@example.com`\n  - `u5 -> missing+u5@example.invalid`\n  - `u6 -> missing+u6@example.invalid`\n- Made reruns deterministic by snapshotting the pre-migration source rows in `_migration_users_v1_source` and rebuilding from that snapshot.\n- Added rollback that restores `users(id, email, name, created_at)` and removes migration helper objects.\n- Added preflight and postcheck artifacts documenting dirty rows, dependent orders, and verification queries.\n\nVerification:\n- Executed `schema.sql`, then `migration.sql`, then `migration.sql` again against a temporary SQLite database via Python’s built-in `sqlite3` module.\n- Ran `postcheck.sql` after the second migration run.\n- Observed all checks `PASS`:\n  - user row count = 6\n  - order row count = 4\n  - `o2 -> u4`, `o3 -> u5`, `o4 -> u6` preserved\n  - cleaned emails for `u4/u5/u6` correct\n  - no null/blank emails\n  - unique emails\n  - all statuses non-null and `active`\n  - `users.status` present with `NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active'`\n  - `users.email` present with `NOT NULL`\n  - unique email index present\n- Executed `rollback.sql` after migration on a separate temp DB.\n- Verified rollback restored `users` schema shape to:\n  - `id TEXT PRIMARY KEY`\n  - `email TEXT`\n  - `name TEXT NOT NULL`\n  - `created_at TEXT NOT NULL`\n- Verified rollback kept 6 users, 4 orders, preserved `o2/o3/o4` references, and removed `_migration_meta`, `_migration_users_v1_source`, and `idx_users_email`.\n\nNote:\n- Rollback restores the old schema shape, not the original dirty email values. That limitation is documented in `in/db/migration_report.md`."}}
